<title>USA: U.S. Nov housing starts rose 9.2 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. Nov housing starts rose 9.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce housing starts and building permits, seasonally adjusted annual rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p> PCT CHANGE: Nov     Oct (Prev)    Sept (Prev)   Nov96/95</p>
<p> -Starts     9.2    -5.1   -5.1    -4.7   -6.1	  3.8</p>
<p> -Permits    3.9    -2.6   -2.7    -1.7   -1.7	 -2.4</p>
<p> RATES	 Nov     Oct (Prev)    Sept (Prev)   Nov 1995</p>
<p> -Starts   1,514   1,386  1,366   1,461  1,440	1,458</p>
<p> -Permits  1,415   1,362  1,361   1,399  1,399	1,450</p>
<p> STARTS:     Nov     Oct (Prev)    Sept (Prev)   Nov 1995</p>
<p> -Single   1,164   1,082  1,069   1,138  1,120	1,129</p>
<p> -Multiple   350     304    297     323    320	  329</p>
<p> PERMITS     Nov     Oct (Prev)    Sept (Prev)   Nov 1995</p>
<p> -Single   1,027   1,011  1,009   1,040  1,040	1,073</p>
<p> -Multiple   388     351    352     359    359	  377</p>
<p> NOV STARTS--Pct--Rate    NOV PERMITS---Pct--Rate--------</p>
<p> -Northeast -2.2   131    -Northeast  -2.2   135</p>
<p> -Midwest   20.8   337    -Midwest     6.7   318</p>
<p> -South     12.0   682    -South	 8.2   635</p>
<p> -West	Unch   364    -West	 -3.5   327</p>
<p>Actual Starts and Permits, unadjusted in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	  Nov     Oct (Prev)    Sept (Prev)   Nov 1995</p>
<p>  Starts     111     131    129     129    127	  107</p>
<p>  Permits    101     126    126     121    121	  108</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast November starts at a 1.39 million unit annual rate.</p>
<p>The department said the November seasonally adjusted gain in housing starts was the largest since an 11.5 percent jump in July 1995.</p>
